<%# The Library — shelf sponsorships, on the main site layout.
    The offer surface, mirroring /dawnfold/sponsors (the house
    model): prices are SHOWN the same way (register price = base +
    house fee pass-through, computed in the route from
    lib/librarySponsors.js), labelled founding rates, inquiries run
    through the site's existing contact machinery (POST /contact,
    topic 'other', the shelf preselected in the message), and NO
    reach / traffic / reader numbers are claimed anywhere — the
    Library is growing and no numbers are printed until provable.
    One difference the honesty rule requires: Dawnfold's rates
    were owner-ordered; these rates are assessed, so they carry the
    extra label "founding rate — pending final confirmation". %>
<h1>Sponsor a Library Shelf</h1>
<p>The Library is the house reading room: public-domain books pulled live from
Project Gutenberg and Standard Ebooks, listening editions from LibriVox, and the
public-domain film shelf Dawnfold's Documentary department draws from. Its books
are bundled in The Library app and read fully offline; the shelves below are its own —
the same shelves the app opens on.</p>
<p>A shelf sponsor takes the <strong>labeled sponsor chair</strong> on one shelf for a
month. The audience is <b>growing</b> and these are <b>founding rates</b> — we don't
print reach numbers we can't prove; when we can prove them, they'll be on this page.</p>

<h2>What a shelf sponsor gets</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>A named, labeled sponsor chair on the shelf</strong> — “<%= 'This shelf is carried by …' %>” with your name on it, printed as a sponsor chair and labelled SPONSOR. Never dressed up as a book, a review, or editorial.</li>
  <li><strong>The chair for a full month</strong> on the shelf you pick, at the founding rate below.</li>
  <li><strong>For the Documentary Shelf,</strong> the chair printed in that department of Dawnfold's edition as well — the shelf and the edition carry the same chair.</li>
  <li><strong>A conversation first.</strong> Every sponsorship starts with an inquiry below; payment is arranged (PayPal, like everything in the house) once we've agreed the run. Nothing is charged by this page.</li>
</ul>
<p class="fineprint">Rates below are founding rates — <b>pending final confirmation</b>
(<%= priceStatus.toLowerCase() %>). The register price shown includes the house
processing-fee pass-through, the same way Dawnfold's rate card shows its prices.</p>

<h2>The shelves</h2>
<% for (const s of shelves) { %>
<section id="shelf-<%= s.key %>" style="border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:12px;padding:1rem;margin:1rem 0;">
  <h3 style="margin-top:0;"><%= s.name %></h3>
  <p><%= s.blurb %></p>
  <% if (s.sponsorEligible) { %>
  <p><strong><%= money(s.priceCents) %></strong> <span>/ <%= s.per %></span>
     · <strong><%= s.availability %></strong>
     · <span>founding rate — pending final confirmation</span></p>
  <%- include('../partials/sponsor-chair', { shelf: s }) %>
  <p><a class="btn" href="#ask" data-shelf="<%= s.name %>">Ask about the <%= s.name %> chair</a></p>
  <% } else { %>
  <p><strong><%= s.availability %>.</strong> No sponsor chairs are sold on this shelf, and it carries no sponsor.</p>
  <% } %>
</section>
<% } %>

<section id="shelf-<%= wholeLibrary.key %>" style="border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:12px;padding:1rem;margin:1rem 0;">
  <h3 style="margin-top:0;"><%= wholeLibrary.name %></h3>
  <p><%= wholeLibrary.blurb %></p>
  <p><strong><%= money(wholeLibrary.priceCents) %></strong> <span>/ <%= wholeLibrary.per %></span>
     · <strong><%= wholeLibrary.availability %></strong>
     · <span>founding rate — pending final confirmation</span></p>
  <p><a class="btn" href="#ask">Ask about the whole-Library chair</a></p>
</section>

<h2 id="ask">Ask about a shelf</h2>
<p>Every sponsorship starts with a conversation — tell us which shelf you're looking
at and we reply from the feedback inbox.</p>
<form method="post" action="/contact" class="stack">
  <input type="text" name="website" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true">
  <input type="hidden" name="topic" value="other">
  <label for="libSpName">Your name / business</label>
  <input id="libSpName" type="text" name="name" required maxlength="120">
  <label for="libSpEmail">Email</label>
  <input id="libSpEmail" type="email" name="email" required maxlength="120">
  <label for="libSpShelf">Which shelf?</label>
  <select id="libSpShelf" name="shelf">
    <% for (const s of shelves) { if (s.sponsorEligible) { %>
    <option value="<%= s.name %>"><%= s.name %></option>
    <% } } %>
    <option value="<%= wholeLibrary.name %>"><%= wholeLibrary.name %></option>
  </select>
  <label for="libSpMsg">Your message</label>
  <textarea id="libSpMsg" name="message" required maxlength="2000" rows="5">Library shelf sponsorship: </textarea>
  <p><button class="btn" type="submit">Send the inquiry</button></p>
</form>
<script>
  // Preselect the shelf in the message when a shelf's Ask link is
  // tapped (progressive enhancement — the select already names it).
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-shelf]').forEach(function (a) {
    a.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var shelf = a.getAttribute('data-shelf');
      var sel = document.getElementById('libSpShelf');
      if (sel) sel.value = shelf;
      var msg = document.getElementById('libSpMsg');
      if (msg) msg.value = 'Library shelf sponsorship: ' + shelf + ' — ';
    });
  });
</script>

<p>From the same house: <a href="/dawnfold">Dawnfold — today's edition</a> ·
<a href="/dawnfold/sponsors">Sponsor Dawnfold</a> ·
<a href="/privacy/library">The Library privacy policy</a> ·
<a href="/apps">Every app</a></p>
<%- include('../partials/sponsor-slot') %>
